invariant: INV-16
file: chacha20_vector.c
catches: chacha20_equiv_test
reason: a group whose counters wrap past 2^32 carries one into the first
  nonce word, as the original ChaCha's 64-bit counter does, where RFC
  8439's counter is 32 bits and chacha20.c's state[12]++ wraps to 0 with
  the nonce unchanged. Only a counter within three of 2^32 reaches the
  edit, so a random counter almost never does, and neither does a record,
  whose counter starts at 1. bin/chacha20_equiv_test's counter-wrap pass
  runs the counter's last values at every length to twenty blocks.

--- old
    x[12] = lanes_counters(counter);
--- new
    x[12] = lanes_counters(counter);
    if (counter > UINT32_MAX - 3) {
        x[13] = lanes_add(x[13], lanes_broadcast(1));
    }
